infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title GOMEMLIMIT: a trap cap vs a budget cap
  desc Same 1.3 GiB live heap — moving the cap from 1.4 to 2 GiB is the whole difference
  compares
    - label Cap 1.4 GiB — trap
      children
        - label ~100 MiB headroom
          desc Live heap sits at 93% of the cap
        - label Cycles run back-to-back
          desc Nothing left for the GC to free
        - label Up to 50% CPU on GC
          desc Runtime's hard cap; the Hook's pod hit 40%+
        - label p99 ~ 900 ms
          desc Collapses while memory graphs stay green
    - label Cap 2.0 GiB — budget
      children
        - label ~700 MiB headroom
          desc The GC has plenty it can free
        - label Cycles spaced by the pacer
          desc ~700 MiB to allocate before re-trigger
        - label ~2% CPU on GC
          desc The gctrace figure for a healthy service
        - label p99 ~ 18 ms
          desc The service's normal latency
theme
  palette #f43f5e #10b981
